Mark the boundaries of the pass being timed, and dump the intervals once it
is over.

VerifyFwSignatureBeforeDecrypt is the first of the install's two decrypts --
the one that reads every chunk of the staged image over QSPI, decrypts it
and hashes the plaintext, and checks the tag only after the loop has run
out.  It is the pass the whole campaign targets
(results/bootloader_spi/PROTOCOL.md section 1).

PassBegin clears the buffer, starts DWT->CYCCNT and PROVES it is running
before anything is recorded; a frozen cycle counter yields intervals of
exactly zero, which reads as a clean constant-time result rather than as a
broken instrument.  PassEnd stops recording and prints.

BOTH CALLS SIT OUTSIDE THE LOOP.  Nothing in this patch prints, allocates
or branches inside the region being timed -- the dump runs after the pass,
on the UART the host is already attached to, because a diagnostic inside the
loop is not a diagnostic: a 1 Hz console line on another rig in this
repository corrupted whole groups of measurements and produced a wrong
conclusion about the instrument that printed it.

PassBegin goes after ST's header-presence check rather than at the top of
the function, so the early return cannot leave a pass open.

Applied by the Makefile's STAGE_RULE with -F0.
--- sfu_fwimg_no_swap.c
+++ sfu_fwimg_no_swap.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 #include "sfu_fwimg_internal.h"
 #include "sfu_trace.h"
 #include "sfu_boot.h"
+#include "sfu_instr.h"
 
 
 #if  defined(SFU_NO_SWAP)
@@ -371,6 +372,8 @@
     return e_ret_status;
   }
 
+  SFU_INSTR_PassBegin(SFU_IMG_CHUNK_SIZE, pFwImageHeader->FwSize);
+
   /* Decryption process initialization
      ================================= */
   se_ret_status = SE_Decrypt_Init(&e_se_status, pFwImageHeader, SE_FW_IMAGE_COMPLETE);
@@ -451,6 +454,8 @@
     e_ret_status = SFU_ERROR;
   }
 
+  SFU_INSTR_PassEnd();
+
   return e_ret_status;
 }
 
